        "## Task 5: Encode Categorical Variables\n",
        "\n",
        "Identify the categorical variables:\n",
        "\n",
        "- `Fuel_Type`\n",
        "- `Seller_Type`\n",
        "- `Transmission`\n",
        "\n",
        "Perform the following:\n",
        "\n",
        "- Convert categorical variables into numerical **dummy/indicator variables**.\n",
        "- Verify that all predictors are numerical after encoding.\n",
        "- Do not assign arbitrary numerical values to categories when such values would imply an incorrect ordering.\n",
        "- Display the transformed dataset.\n",
        "\n",
        "---"
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "U1eOofspGacW"
      }
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "# TASK 5: ENCODE CATEGORICAL VARIABLES\n",
        "\n",
        "# Make a copy of the dataset\n",
        "df_encoded = df.copy()\n",
        "\n",
        "# Identify categorical variables\n",
        "categorical_columns = [\n",
        "    \"Fuel_Type\",\n",
        "    \"Seller_Type\",\n",
        "    \"Transmission\"\n",
        "]\n",
        "\n",
        "# Check which categorical columns are actually present\n",
        "available_categorical_columns = [\n",
        "    column for column in categorical_columns\n",
        "    if column in df_encoded.columns\n",
        "]\n",
        "\n",
        "print(\"Categorical variables found:\")\n",
        "print(available_categorical_columns)\n",
        "\n",
        "# Convert categorical variables into dummy/indicator variables\n",
        "df_encoded = pd.get_dummies(\n",
        "    df_encoded,\n",
        "    columns=available_categorical_columns,\n",
        "    drop_first=True,\n",
        "    dtype=int\n",
        ")\n",
        "\n",
        "# Display the transformed dataset\n",
        "print(\"\\nTransformed dataset:\")\n",
        "display(df_encoded.head())\n",
        "\n",
        "# Verify that all columns are numerical\n",
        "non_numeric_columns = df_encoded.select_dtypes(\n",
        "    exclude=[\"number\"]\n",
        ").columns.tolist()\n",
        "\n",
        "print(\"\\nNon-numerical columns after encoding:\")\n",
        "print(non_numeric_columns)\n",
        "\n",
        "if len(non_numeric_columns) == 0:\n",
        "    print(\"\\nSUCCESS: All predictors are numerical after encoding.\")\n",
        "else:\n",
        "    print(\"\\nWARNING: Some non-numerical columns still exist.\")\n",
        "\n",
        "# Display final column names\n",
        "print(\"\\nFinal columns after encoding:\")\n",
        "print(df_encoded.columns.tolist())\n",
        "\n",
        "# Create final predictor matrix X and target vector y\n",
        "target_column = \"Selling_Price\"\n",
        "\n",
        "# Handle possible column-name variation\n",
        "if target_column not in df_encoded.columns:\n",
        "    matching_columns = [\n",
        "        column for column in df_encoded.columns\n",
        "        if column.lower().replace(\" \", \"_\") == \"selling_price\"\n",
        "    ]\n",
        "\n",
        "    if len(matching_columns) > 0:\n",
        "        target_column = matching_columns[0]\n",
        "    else:\n",
        "        raise ValueError(\"Selling_Price column was not found.\")\n",
        "\n",
        "X = df_encoded.drop(columns=[target_column]).astype(float).values\n",
        "y = df_encoded[target_column].astype(float).values\n",
        "\n",
        "print(\"\\nFinal predictor matrix X shape:\", X.shape)\n",
        "print(\"Final target vector y shape:\", y.shape)\n",
        "\n",
        "print(\"\\nTask 5 completed successfully!\")"
